 ],
 "literal": "With the sea playing and in the seashore grove staying / with the garlanded playmates the beauty of embrace performing / like strangers suddenly having come / he embraced, if he goes, gossip arose indeed / beauty spots spread beautiful wide waist / perfect jewels swaying branch tied green sprout / even than the leaf-garment from her side he does not go away / he himself gave, mother guarding and protecting.",
 "translation": "We played in the sea and stayed in the seashore grove, celebrating the joy of embraces with our garlanded playmates. If he had come suddenly like a stranger, embraced her, and then departed, gossip would have surely arisen. But now, he does not stir from her side, closer than the garment of fresh green leaves tied to the swaying branches that drapes her beautiful wide waist adorned with perfect jewels and beauty spots. He has given her back to us himself, and mother now guards her with care.",
 "modern": "கடலில் விளையாடியும் கடற்கரைச் சோலையில் தங்கியும், மாலை அணிந்த தோழியருடன் தழுவி விளையாடி மகிழ்ந்தோம். அயலாரைப் போல அவன் திடீரென்று வந்து அவளைத் தழுவிவிட்டுச் சென்றிருந்தால், ஊரில் அலர் (பழிச்சொல்) தூற்றியிருக்கும். ஆனால், அழகிய தேமல் பரவிய, அகன்ற அல்குலில், திருத்தமான அணிகலன்களோடு, அசையும் மரக்கிளையிலிருந்து பறித்துக் கட்டிய பசிய தழையாடையை விடவும் அவளை விட்டு நீங்காமல் அவளருகிலேயே அவன் இருக்கிறான். அவனே அவளை எங்களிடம் ஒப்படைத்துவிட்டான்; இப்போது தாயும் அவளைப் பாதுகாத்துக் காக்கிறாள்.",
 "explanation": "The confidante speaks to the hero, expressing relief that public gossip has been averted. She recalls how they used to play in the sea and seashore groves with their companions. If the hero had behaved like a fleeting stranger, embracing the heroine and leaving, rumors would have ruined her reputation. However, he has proven his commitment by staying constantly by her side, closer than the very leaf-garment she wears. Since he has formally returned her to her family's care, the mother now guards her safely at home, paving the way for an honorable marriage.",
